<p>This week's chapter: <a href="/how-to-build-an-ai/prove-it-got-better/">Prove it got better</a>. Your agent feels better than what you started with, and this is how you find out whether it actually is. You ask it the same ten questions twice, change one thing between the runs, and count what comes back. Two numbers, side by side, and an honest answer either way. <strong>The film goes live later this week.</strong> The written chapter has every step in the meantime, and it stands on its own.</p>

<p>Hi, and welcome. If you're curious how an AI actually gets built, and whether <em>you</em> could build one, this is a good place to start. This guide grows a chapter at a time, and you can read it at your own pace. You don't need any coding experience, and you don't need to finish all of it. Think of it as a gentle on-ramp, not a test.</p>

